       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg/day, which is 10 times the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults. A single 8000 mg dose could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant **800 mg** instead of 8000 mg. Typical adult oral dosing is:\n- **400\u2013800 mg per dose, 3\u20134 times daily**\n- **Maximum 3200 mg/day** in a monitored setting, and usually 2400 mg/day or less\n- Take it with food, and use the lowest effective dose for the shortest time\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. For example, if you meant ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day), I can enter that right away. You may also want to ask your senior resident or pharmacist whether that total daily dose suits this patient. Many clinicians would choose 600 mg or 800 mg three times daily instead."
